{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "e6e429ad-2403-8628-84d8-216b4bdfc9de",
  "created_at": "2026-03-10T11:07:10-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Canvassing",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Anthony M. Grasso",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Walter Tavares",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:05:17-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Canvassing, this is Walter. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:05:21-04:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, Walter. My name is Anthony Grasso. I'm calling for my mother. She's in her eighties and she'd like to vote by mail. So, first, how does she request a mail ballot? Second, does she have to send anything with it? And third, how long does it take to come?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:05:37-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. Is your mother a registered voter here in Newport?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:05:41-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. She's been registered at the same place for decades."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:05:45-04:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. She'll need to fill out a mail ballot application. You can get the form from the state elections website, or we can mail one to her from this office. She signs it herself and returns it to us here or to the state. Once it's processed, the ballot gets mailed out."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:06:01-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. First, can you mail the application to her house? Second, can I pick it up for her instead? I'm in town."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:06:08-04:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Either one works. You can stop by the office at City Hall during business hours and pick one up, or I can put one in the mail today if you give me her name and the address she's registered at."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:06:21-04:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me think. I'll come by and get one. Now, what ID is required? I want to be sure I have everything. [pause] Sorry, hold on, my smartwatch just buzzed. It says I hit my step goal. Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:06:34-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. For a mail ballot application, she'll usually be asked for a driver's license or other ID number on the form, and then a copy of the ID may be needed with the ballot itself. I'd check the instructions on the form, because it spells out what's accepted."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:06:49-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So, first, the ID number goes on the application. Second, a copy of the ID goes with the ballot. Third, the form lists what's accepted."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:06:57-04:00",
      "duration": 1,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:06:58-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good. Then I'll come by this afternoon. Thank you, Walter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:07:02-04:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Mr. Grasso. We're open until the end of the afternoon. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-10T11:07:08-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
